@page "/"
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
<PageTitle>Home</PageTitle>

<div class="container py-4">
    <h3 class="mb-4">Hazard Dice Web Game</h3>

    <p>
        Hazard is an early English dice game that dates back to the 14th century.
        Most popular in the gaming clubs of 17th and 18th century London, Hazard
        derives its name from the risk associated with its unforgiving rules and
        bets placed on the outcome of the game. This game is played with two dice
        and the rules are as follows:
    </p>

    <h5 class="mt-4">Rules</h5>
    <ul class="mb-4">
        <li>
            <strong>Main declaration:</strong> One participant—the caster—announces a
            <em>main</em>, a target number from 5 to 9, then rolls two dice.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>First roll:</strong> Rolling the main is an immediate win (“nicking”),
            while rolling a 2 or 3 is an immediate loss (“throwing out”). Outcomes of 11
            or 12 vary by main (e.g., on a main of 7, an 11 wins but a 12 loses).
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Subsequent rolls:</strong> If the first roll is neither win nor loss,
            that total becomes the <em>chance</em>. The caster keeps rolling until they roll
            either the chance (a win) or the main (a loss).
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h5 class="mt-4">Game Adaptation</h5>
    <p>
        For this application, we’ve adapted the traditional rules slightly. Instead of
        choosing a main up front, the caster simply rolls the dice until a valid main
        (5–9) appears, and that value becomes the main for the rest of the round.
    </p>

    <strong>Click on the "Hazard Game" tab in the navigation menu to start playing!</strong>
</div>
